{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"205","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B. Little Elephant and Sorting"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"0.5 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The Little Elephant loves sortings."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"He has an array "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a"},{"kind":"text","text":" consisting of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" integers. Let's number the array elements from 1 to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":", then the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th element will be denoted as "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ai"},{"kind":"text","text":". The Little Elephant can make one move to choose an arbitrary pair of integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"l"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"r"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(1 ≤ l ≤ r ≤ n)"},{"kind":"text","text":" and increase "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ai"},{"kind":"text","text":" by "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" for all "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":" such that "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"l ≤ i ≤ r"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Help the Little Elephant find the minimum number of moves he needs to convert array "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a"},{"kind":"text","text":" to an arbitrary array sorted in the non-decreasing order. Array "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a"},{"kind":"text","text":", consisting of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" elements, is sorted in the non-decreasing order if for any "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(1 ≤ i < n)"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ai ≤ ai + 1"},{"kind":"text","text":" holds."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains a single integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(1 ≤ n ≤ 105)"},{"kind":"text","text":" — the size of array "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a"},{"kind":"text","text":". The next line contains "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" integers, separated by single spaces — array "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(1 ≤ ai ≤ 109)"},{"kind":"text","text":". The array elements are listed in the line in the order of their index's increasing."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In a single line print a single integer — the answer to the problem."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Please, do not use the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"%lld"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" specifier to read or write 64-bit integers in С++. It is preferred to use the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cin"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cout"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" streams or the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"%I64d"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" specifier."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"3\n1 2 3\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"0\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"3\n3 2 1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"2\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"4\n7 4 1 47\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"6\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first sample the array is already sorted in the non-decreasing order, so the answer is "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"0"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second sample you need to perform two operations: first increase numbers from second to third (after that the array will be: "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"[3, 3, 2]"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"), and second increase only the last element (the array will be: "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"[3, 3, 3]"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":")."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the third sample you should make at least 6 steps. The possible sequence of the operations is: "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"(2; 3), (2; 3), (2; 3), (3; 3), (3; 3), (3; 3)"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". After that the array converts to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"[7, 7, 7, 47]"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"B","problemCode":"205B","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/205/problem/B"}